caption: $:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate
title: PanelTemplate

! Summary

Dual-context sections (rendering in BOTH the panel and the new-item modal) live in `ui/attributes/` and carry BOTH tags plus BOTH group tags — the chassis of each context provides `section-target`/`section-type`/`section-mode`, and a single body serves both (write-once, tagged twice). Single-context sections keep `ui/panel/` or `ui/modal/`. Naming revisit-trigger: if a future dual section is not an item attribute, reconsider the `ui/attributes` name.
Add a section to the attributes panel shown on item tiddlers.

! Detail
Tag a tiddler with `$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate` to make it a panel section. Give it a `caption` field for the section legend. Additionally tag it with a portion tag to place it (untagged members land in Portion/1):

| !Portion tag | !Position |
|$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/Top |Full width above the portions (picker label: "Top, full-width") |
|$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/1 |First (only) portion |
|$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/N |Nth portion — portions sit side by side; a portion exists the moment a section claims it |
|$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/Full |Full width below the portions (picker label: "Bottom, full-width") |

Set portions from the Settings → Panel and modal Portion picker beside each row, or by tag — the picker always offers one number beyond the highest in use, so a new portion is one pick away. The same vocabulary applies to modal sections and dashboard lists.

Sections render inside a `<fieldset>`; gate content with `is[current]` type tags so sections only apply to relevant types:

```
title: $:/plugins/MyPlugin/ui/panel/due-date
caption: Due
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

<%if [is[current]tag[$:/GSD/Action]] %>
  …section content…
<%endif%>
```

The view's placement (above/below the body) is configurable per type via the [[ViewPlacement|ViewPlacement]] tag list (`$:/config/hypergsd/Placement/*`); the orientation within a group (stacked or flowing) is the `$:/config/hypergsd/panel-layout` setting (Panel and modal tab, shared with the modal).

! Folding

Panel sections participate in TiddlyWiki's per-tiddler folding. The panel chassis passes the tiddler's core fold state (`$:/state/folded/<title>` — the same tiddler, with the same orientation, as the body's own reveal) into the portions engine, and every section whose folded visibility is Hidden renders inside a `<$reveal>` keyed on that state. Fold a tiddler with the fold bar or the fold toolbar button and the body and the Hidden sections fold together; sections set to Shown stay visible. The core fold bar ships hidden in TiddlyWiki — enable it under Settings → Toolbars → view toolbar buttons (this wiki ships it enabled).

Each section's folded visibility is set per section in Settings → Panel and modal → Panel sections ("Visibility when tiddler is folded"), stored as `show`/`hide` at `$:/config/hypergsdPanel/folded/<section title>`, defaulting to `hide`. Status and Complete ship as `show`; hypergsd-priorities ships its Priority section as `show` from its own config. The modal never folds — its sections render regardless of the host tiddler's fold state.

! Lists fold too

Folding is generic at the lists chassis: `hgsd-dashboard-portions` wraps its whole output (bands, portions, lists) in a reveal keyed on the host's core fold state, so ''every'' host folds with its tiddler — dashboard pages, the project view (a folded project tiddler shows its panel card and nothing else), the contact view, and the hand-rolled context view. No configuration and no per-host wiring: a new dashboard page or view host gets folding by rendering through the chassis.

! Folding for section authors

A shipped panel section needs ''no work'' to participate: it folds away with the tiddler by default, and its Settings row grows the folded-visibility select automatically. Three things to know:

* ''Stay-visible sections'' ship a config shadow titled `$:/config/hypergsdPanel/folded/<section title>` with text `show` (body without a trailing newline — the config-shadow rule; see [[Fields and State]]). That is exactly how Status and Complete ship theirs (`ui/config/panel-fold/defaults.multids`). A sub-plugin ships its own file the same way, so the default travels with the plugin — hypergsd-priorities ships its Priority section as `show` (`hypergsd-priorities/ui/config/panel-fold/defaults.multids`).
* ''One extra wrapper div.'' In the panel, a foldable section's content sits inside `div.hgsd-fold-slot` (the reveal). Styles keyed on your section's own classes are unaffected; a selector reaching ''down'' from the portion container (`.hgsd-capture > div > …`) gains one level in panels. Modal and dashboard renderings have no wrapper.
* ''No refresh declaration.'' The reveal reads core's `$:/state/folded/` prefix, which the panel and placement-slot gates already admit — nothing to add to `hgsd-refresh-whitelist`. A sub-plugin hosting its ''own'' panel chassis (its own `hgsd-section-portions` call with `fold-state`) must admit `[prefix[$:/state/folded/]]` in its own gate; without `fold-state` a chassis simply never folds (the modal and every dashboard).

! Best Practice
Interactive controls: standard widgets carry their own handling; raw `<input>`/`<button>` elements only work for the plugin's `data-hgsd-*` actions via the event delegation — new actions require extending the event handler module.